# Keep the build context to source. Two entries here are about secrecy rather
# than size, and both matter more than the rest put together.

# The keys. Seven provider accounts plus LangSmith and Tavily live here, and
# none of them belongs in an image layer -- they are environment variables at
# run time (docs/17-deployment.md#176-what-has-to-change-first). Listed even
# though it is gitignored: a build context is the working tree, not the index.
llm_router/.env
**/.env
*.pem
*.key

# What this machine's accounts have spent. Baking a ledger into the image would
# ship one developer's consumption to every container that ever runs it, and
# the running container mounts a volume here instead.
llm_router/.usage/

.git/
.gitignore
.github/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Run output: megabytes of log per run, none of it needed to serve.
evals/results/runs/
evals/results/reviews/
.claude/

# Prose. The wiki is how a human understands the system and no process in the
# container reads it.
#
# `*.md` is root-level only -- a pattern's `*` does not cross `/` -- which is
# why the prompts survive it. They are **not** prose: every agent reads its
# Markdown under `agent/` at run time, so an image without them starts and then
# fails on the first task. The negations below say so out loud, so that
# broadening this to `**/*.md` fails the build instead of a run.
docs/
*.md
!agent/code/prompts/*.md
!agent/runtime/prompts/*.md
!agent/explore/prompts/*.md
!agent/explore/tool_descriptions/*.md

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
